  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There is a rooted tree of NNN vertices rooted at vertex 111. Each vertex vvv has a value AvA_vAv​ associated with it.\n\nYou choose a vertex vvv (possibly the root) from the tree and remove all vertices on the path from the root to the vertex vvv, also including vvv. This will result in a forest of zero or more connected components.\n\nThe beauty of a connected component is the GCD\\mathrm{GCD}GCD of the values of all vertices in the component. Find the maximum value of the sum of beauties of the obtained connected components for any choice of vvv.\n\nHere, GCD\\mathrm{GCD}GCD stands for Greatest Common Divisor.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the size of the tree.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the values associated with each vertex.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines contain two space-separated integers uuu and vvv — denoting an undirected edge between nodes uuu and vvv.\n\nIt is guaranteed that the edges given in the input form a tree.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case output the maximum value of the sum of beauties of the obtained connected components for any choice of vvv.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 2\\cdot10^41≤T≤2⋅104",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤u,v≤N1 \\leq u,v \\leq N1≤u,v≤N and u≠vu \\neq vu=v",
      "It is guaranteed that the edges given in the input form a tree.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot10^53⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n10\n15 30 15 5 3 15 3 3 5 5\n1 2\n1 5\n2 3\n2 4\n5 6\n5 7\n5 8\n7 9\n7 10",
        "output": "33",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe tree from the sample is as follows.\n![tree_basic](https://s3.amazonaws.com/codechef_shared/download/Images/the_hyp0cr1t3/tree_basic.png =450x450)\nIf vertex v=7v = 7v=7 is chosen, vertices 111, 555 and 777 are removed.\n![tree_remove](https://s3.amazonaws.com/codechef_shared/download/Images/the_hyp0cr1t3/tree_remove.png =450x450)\nThe resulting forest contains five connected components {8},{6},{10},{9}\\{8\\}, \\{6\\}, \\{10\\}, \\{9\\}{8},{6},{10},{9} and {2,3,4}\\{2, 3, 4\\}{2,3,4}.\n![tree_value](https://s3.amazonaws.com/codechef_shared/download/Images/the_hyp0cr1t3/tree_value.png =450x450)\nThe beauties of the connected components are 333, 151515, 555, 555 and 555 respectively. Thus the answer is 3+15+5+5+5=333 + 15 + 5 + 5 + 5 = 333+15+5+5+5=33.\nIt can be shown that this is the maximum value possible for any choice of vvv."
      }
    ]
  },
